proof: redumper-mpf | opensuse | vendor-cap
date: 2026-07-17
lane/VM: test-openSUSE (openSUSE Leap 16.0), repo OBS home:gmipf:media-preservation/16.0
user groups: "gmipf wheel" (NO cdrom/disk/plugdev) -> groupless
drive: PLEXTOR DVDR PX-760A (USB 0dc4:0061) -> /dev/sr1, audio CD (20 tracks)
mechanism: openSUSE permissions framework (permctl) via %set_permissions in
           opensuse/redumper-mpf/redumper-mpf.spec
note: fixed-name pin (was redumper732); binary moved to /usr/bin/redumper-mpf, so
      the permissions.d entry targets a different path and this line was re-measured.

--- delivery (as installed from OBS via zypper, never hand-touched) ---
zypper install output (permctl setting the cap at install time):
  /usr/bin/redumper-mpf: setting to root:root 0755 "cap_sys_rawio=ep". (missing capabilities)
$ /usr/sbin/getcap /usr/bin/redumper-mpf
/usr/bin/redumper-mpf cap_sys_rawio=ep
$ rpm -qf /usr/bin/redumper-mpf -> redumper-mpf-732-lp160.4.1.x86_64
$ /usr/bin/redumper-mpf --version -> redumper (build: b732)
$ rpm -V redumper-mpf -> "........P  /usr/bin/redumper-mpf"
  (expected on openSUSE: the header may not carry %caps, permctl sets it at
   install, so header != disk is normal -- NOT a defect.)

--- GREEN (cap present): D8 vendor read reaches the drive ---
$ redumper-mpf disc --verbose --drive=/dev/sr1 --image-path=... --image-name=t
  inquiry: PLEXTOR - DVDR PX-760A (revision level: 1.07, vendor specific: 08/18/07 15:10)
  configuration: PLEXTOR (read offset: +30, C2 shift: 295, pre-gap start: -75,
                 read method: D8, sector order: DATA_C2_SUB)
  lead-in reads (negative LBA, via D8) = 75, "Operation not permitted" = 0,
  lines with "SCSIs: [1-9]" = 0
  last progress: / [  7%] LBA:  20476/277131, errors: { SCSIs: 0, C2s: 0, Q: 36 }
  (run trimmed by `timeout 50`, exit 124)

--- RED (A/B: cap stripped with `setcap -r`, then restored) ---
$ sudo setcap -r /usr/bin/redumper-mpf ; /usr/sbin/getcap -> ''      # cap gone
$ redumper-mpf disc ... (same command)
- [  0%] LBA:    -75/277131, errors: { SCSIs: 0, C2s: 0, Q: 0 }error: SYSTEM (Operation not permitted)
  exit 255 ; "Operation not permitted" hits = 1     # EPERM at the first D8 read
$ sudo setcap cap_sys_rawio=ep /usr/bin/redumper-mpf ; getcap -> cap_sys_rawio=ep   # restored

VERDICT: PROVEN. permctl delivers the cap on the renamed binary at install time and
it is load-bearing: with it the D8 lead-in read (-75..-1) succeeds groupless;
without it the identical read fails EPERM at LBA -75.
